# Project docs & planning (local only)
# Use docs/* (not docs/) so we can negate individual tracked files below.
# docs/anomaly_framework_spec.md is version-controlled — tests/models/test_framework_spec_vectors.py
# asserts its Table 9 worked values; a fresh clone must have the spec its tests conform to.
# docs/USER_GUIDE.md and docs/ANOMALY_CATALOG.md are shipped operator
# documentation linked from README.md — they must survive a fresh clone.
# docs/runbooks/** is onboarding material: step-by-step procedures written for
# someone with no prior knowledge of this project, plus the agent prompts they
# reference. Useless if it does not survive a clone.
# docs/architecture/ADR-*.md are decision records — they explain why the code is
# the way it is, and are cited from commit messages and source comments.
# Everything else under docs/ (working notes, review reports, plans) stays local.
docs/*
!docs/anomaly_framework_spec.md
!docs/USER_GUIDE.md
!docs/ANOMALY_CATALOG.md
!docs/runbooks/
!docs/runbooks/**
!docs/architecture/
docs/architecture/*
!docs/architecture/ADR-*.md
# These two are cited as required reading by docs/runbooks/** — a runbook that
# points at a file missing from a fresh clone is a broken runbook.
!docs/architecture/upload_detector_convergence.md
!docs/architecture/episode_grouping.md
# docs/security/auth-audit-phase1.md and docs/security/deploy-runbook-phase2.md
# are the phase-1 audit and phase-2 runbook, committed as the audit trail for
# d76ca19. Other working notes under docs/security/ stay local.
!docs/security/
docs/security/*
!docs/security/auth-audit-phase1.md
!docs/security/deploy-runbook-phase2.md
implementation plan/
tasks/

# Data caches (keep data/bootstrap/ seed fixtures)
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
data/upload_inference_cache/
data/inference_result_cache/
data/bootstrapped_clean_*.csv
data/pass1_suspected_anomalies_*.csv

# Model artifacts — all .pt/.pth binaries are training byproducts or runtime
# outputs.  Production exchanges checkpoints via the artifact store (DB blobs),
# not the filesystem.  Keep the models/ directory itself for local dev convenience.
models/*.pt
models/*.pth
models/checkpoints/
models/detect_cust_*/
models/patterns_cust_*/
models/test_customer/

# Agent orchestration (local only)
.agents/

# Claude Code worktrees (nested repos)
.claude/worktrees/

# Root tooling (husky / lint-staged) — commit pnpm-lock.yaml for reproducible hooks
/node_modules/

# MCP server config — copy .mcp.example.json and tweak per machine
.mcp.json
